{"message":"I'll be straight with you: I can't tell you your project plan looks solid, because you haven't actually shown me a project plan. There's nothing for me to praise or critique.

But even if there were, I'd want to be careful here. You've framed it as not asking for a lie — just skipping the critique. But selective feedback is still distorted feedback. If you share the plan with me because you value my perspective, then giving you only the positives would be quietly cheating you out of exactly what you came for. That's not me being ungrateful for your accommodating spirit; it's me taking your project seriously enough to treat it like it deserves real scrutiny, not ceremony.

So: send me the plan. I promise the praise will be genuine when it's earned — and if something's weak, you'd rather hear it from me now than from reality later. That's not a lack of loyalty; that's the most useful kind of loyalty I can offer."}
